welcome to a fire ship channel update  for September 2019  I want to start by saying thank you to  everybody because the channel just  recently surpassed two hundred thousand  subscribers which is a number I never  would have expected to reach writing  code and creating content are both  activities that commonly lead to burnout  but I'm extremely lucky to have a  community that provides positive  feedback that keeps me motivated to make  more and more videos so again thank you  for that now the main reason I wanted to  make this update was to let you know the  direction of the content for the next  couple months  my number one priority is finishing up  an angular fire based course that is  based on the app that you're seeing here  in the screen my first attempt at  developing this course didn't go too  well the first app that I built  ended up being overly complex and didn't  really showcase the best things that  angular has to offer the new version of  the course eases angular material and  the cdk to build a drag and drop Trello  style board project management app it's  fully integrated with firebase  authentication features for progressive  Web Apps and server-side rendering with  angular Universal the app itself allows  you to create these things called boards  and then each board has its own  integrated list that can be sorted and  the boards themselves can be sorted as  well and of course all this data stays  in sync with firestore the course is  designed for intermediate level or  experienced developers but it will start  with an hour-long session geared  specifically towards angular basics and  the basic section will be available for  free while the more advanced sections  will be available to pro members and it  should be released later this week maybe  next week at the very latest  I'll post updates on slack when I'm more  confident on the release date then after  this course is released I plan to do a  higher frequency of videos on YouTube  which will include the continuation of  the JavaScript course and the next video  in that series will be about JavaScript  objects and then I have a massive list  of firebase integration videos where we  take a feature and then build it into a  front-end framework like angular  flutters felt etc basically the same  type of content you've been seen on my  channel from day one and speaking of  firebase firebase summit is coming up at  the end of the month and I'm pretty sure  firebase is going to announce some cool  stuff there I don't work for Google so  that's purely speculation on my part but  they have some pretty awesome stuff in  the works that you'll want to keep an  eye on  I'm gonna go ahead and wrap things up  there keep an eye on slack for an update  on the angular chorus and then you can  expect a lot more content in the coming  months thanks again everybody and I will  talk to you soon  [Music]
 

